   "fix": "Guard the forward lemma, as Mathlib does for this pattern: `simp [-singletVector_dotProduct, \u2190 singletVector_dotProduct, dotProduct, sum_univ, Finset.sum_add_distrib]`, or use an explicit `simp only` list that never reintroduces `singlet`.",
   "issue": "`singlet_apply` is proved by `simp [\u2190 singletVector_dotProduct, dotProduct, sum_univ, Finset.sum_add_distrib]`, but `singletVector_dotProduct` (line 180-182) is `@[simp]` in the forward direction, so the same simp call carries `singlet v \u2192 singletVector \u2b1d\u1d65 v` and `singletVector \u2b1d\u1d65 v \u2192 singlet v`. It closes today only because the `dotProduct` unfolding happens to fire first; any priority or simp-set change flips it into a loop.",
